## Round 5 correction (after /review re-review of dd3cd3e7f)
The round-4 C2 mutation above was not the bare JS multiply: it also put back a float magnitude for a count, so it proved nothing about total_cost alone. Two reviewers reverted only the multiply and it survived: 0.05 x 0.5 is 0.025 in float too. A case where the float product lands below the half cent (0.03 x 5.5 = 0.16499999999999998) was added, on a decrease and on a count. The bare mutation now goes red:
```
### C2 (corrected) total_cost multiplied in JS float, integer-cents magnitude left in place
   × total_cost is multiplied in SQL NUMERIC: 0.03 x 5.5 = 0.165 -> 0.17 on a decrease and on a count 45ms
⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯ Failed Tests 1 ⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯
      Tests  1 failed | 19 passed (20)
```
